  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Mikania cordata",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mikania_cordata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1209522268,
      "text": "Mikania cordata, the African mile-a-minute or heartleaf hempvine, is a species of flowering plant in the family Asteraceae, disjunctly distributed across the Old World Tropics. A perennial twining vine reaching 10 m (33 ft) long, it grows in thickets and forests at elevations from 100 to 1,700 m, at least in China. It is a rapidly-growing climber that suppresses the growth of other plants and is considered a more dangerous noxious weed than Mikania micrantha. Local peoples occasionally consume its leaves and use it for erosion control."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Sembung rambat",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sembung_rambat",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 29668802,
      "text": "Sembung rambat adalah tumbuhan merambat (climber) dan termasuk ke dalam keluarga Asteraceae. Tumbuhan ini mempunyai bunga berwarna putih-keunguan dan memiliki harum yang kuat, umumnya ditemukan di hutan sekunder, tanah telantar, pinggir jalan, jurang dan dapat mencegah erosi. Tumbuhan ini terdistribusi Afrika, Asia hingga Papua Nugini. Di Indonesia, tumbuhan ini terdapat salah satunya di Gunung Prau."
    }
  },
